From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:43:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpio: apple,d2365-pmic-gpio: Add the D2255

The D2255 (Antigua) is the PMIC of the Samsung A9 iPhone 6s and 6s
Plus. It has 21 GPIO lines with the D2333's configuration byte layout.
Its PMU events are not described yet, so like the D2186 and D2333 it is
a GPIO controller only.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml     | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
index 1a5a8c167..83b7a00c3 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
@@ -11,8 +11,8 @@ maintainers:
 
 description: |
   The Dialog D2186 and D2207 PMICs used with the Apple A8 and A8X and the
-  D2333 and D2365 PMICs used in Apple A9 and A10 devices provide 21, 21, 21
-  and 24 GPIOs respectively. The controller is accessed through the regmap exported by the
+  D2255, D2333 and D2365 PMICs used in Apple A9 and A10 devices provide 21,
+  21, 21, 21 and 24 GPIOs respectively. The controller is accessed through the regmap exported by the
   parent Apple I2C PMIC device.
 
   The D2207 and D2365 also latch 112 and 240 PMU events respectively
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ properties:
       - apple,d2089-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2186-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2207-pmic-gpio
+      - apple,d2255-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2333-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2365-pmic-gpio
 
@@ -108,6 +109,7 @@ allOf:
         compatible:
           enum:
             - apple,d2186-pmic-gpio
+            - apple,d2255-pmic-gpio
             - apple,d2333-pmic-gpio
     then:
       properties:
